{"is_error":false,"duration_api_ms":221494,"num_turns":15,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"0a2586ba-49dc-458d-9a82-ed6a30a99f7c","total_cost_usd":1.5916275,"usage":{"input_tokens":24,"cache_creation_input_tokens":73889,"cache_read_input_tokens":964235,"output_tokens":14820,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":73889,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":668,"cache_read_input_tokens":92229,"cache_creation_input_tokens":610,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":610},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5":{"inputTokens":24,"outputTokens":14820,"cacheReadInputTokens":964235,"cacheCreationInputTokens":73889,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":1.5916275,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5","provider":"firstParty"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"extra_usage_disabled","subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"**Task `spike-live-transport` — handed back to Codex, no README written. Commit `fc252ef` (state file only).**\n\nPlain-English summary of why:\n\nThe brief told me to check four things in the repo before writing. Three were true. One was not.\n\n`dispatch.sh` says in its header comment: *exit code 0 is the only success, and it means the loop reached `turn: operator`*. That is not what the script does. Two paths exit 0 without the loop ever running:\n\n- `--dry-run` — checks things, says which actor it *would* start, starts nothing, exits 0. I proved this in a throwaway sandbox: a file at `turn: codex` came back exit 0 and unchanged.\n- `--help` — prints usage, exits 0.\n\nThe README was required to say what every exit code means, using only what the scripts support. Exit 0 means one thing in a real run and a different thing in dry-run. I could not write that down without quietly picking a winner, and the brief specifically said not to do that — hand it back instead. So the unit did not start: no README, no other file touched.\n\nTwo side notes I recorded but did not act on: the default `--allow-path` values are not documented in the usage header, and one error path reuses the `BAD_TURN` code for a different situation (unreachable in practice).\n\nOne useful accident: when I first tried a dry-run against this task, it exited 17 — *another dispatcher holds this task*. That is the live dispatcher that launched me. So the transport you were trying to observe is working.\n\nCodex now decides whether the comment or the code is right. If the code is right, the README gets written and the stale comment line is a separate item. If the comment is right, the fix is in `dispatch.sh`, which this task's scope excludes — that would need you to reopen the scope.","ttft_ms":8684,"ttft_stream_ms":8098,"time_to_request_ms":39,"type":"result","duration_ms":273276,"uuid":"5ac3d327-6d9b-42c9-900f-387f30187382"}
